From a2d3ce43178ed65b1e9b28c1b4d26c8b92cba057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:49:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(ewm): supersession uses the statement's holder, not
 its first capitalised word

Ewm1Memory.replaces() compared Ewm1Fact.subject, i.e. the first capitalised
nominal. For first-person facts that is the city ('Ich wohne in Wien.' ->
wien) or a sentence-initial adverb ('Inzwischen wohne ich in Graz.' ->
inzwischen), so the speaker's relocation never superseded the old residence.

Supersession only (subject, answers and every other rule are unchanged):
- holder: 'ich'/'wir' when the first clause has that nominative pronoun and it
  is not coordinated; otherwise the first mention that is no sentence-initial
  update/time adverb.
- relationGroups: a kinship word naming the holder ('Meine Schwester ist ...')
  is no shared relation.
- the holder's own apposition name is no shared other entity.
- statements of disjoint thesaurus relations never replace each other.
- the speaker path needs a shared relation; a shared city or date is not enough.

Host evidence: new test 19/19 (red before: 8/19 fail); 769/769 host JUnit over
148+1 android-free test classes incl. Ewm2ProductEquivalenceTest; adversarial
grid of 6720 pairs TP 120->348, FP 183->48, FN 228->0, bystanders lost 0.
Residual: a third person's past visit can be marked outdated by a later state
(48/6720); no validity interval is stored. Not built for Android, not on Fold7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016mth9YBUvdbdA8HPpwcwN6
---
