From b24253411608807b8b2416fb191c958d50b5e3ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:59:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(ewm): a state that starts in the future does not
 supersede the present one
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The holder fix let 'Ab nächstem Monat wohne ich in Graz.' supersede 'Ich wohne
in Wien.' at once (single-valued 'wohnen'), so the present residence was
reported outdated before the move. A later residence/work statement with a
future cue (demnächst, bald, künftig, nächste/n/m/r/s, übermorgen) no longer
supersedes; no start date is derived. Appointments postponed to 'nächsten
Mittwoch' still replace the old date (zeitpunkt path, test added).

Red before this commit: 1/22 (the future move); after: 22/22. Host regression
772/772. Grid with the future form, 7872 pairs: FP 195->48, FN 228->0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016mth9YBUvdbdA8HPpwcwN6
